To fix this, the application must implement strict output encoding. This means converting special characters like '<' and '>' into their HTML entity equivalents ('&lt;' and '&gt;') so the browser treats them as plain text instead of executable code. Additionally, the 'HttpOnly' flag should be set on all session cookies to prevent JavaScript from accessing them via 'document.cookie'.

Fixed Code (PHP):
